<title>USA: GENICOM sees higher Q4 revs, net.</title>
<headline>GENICOM sees higher Q4 revs, net.</headline>
<dateline>CHANTILLY, Va. 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>GENICOM Corp said on Wednesday that it expects fourth quarter earnings per share between $0.16 and $0.18 and sales between $89 million and $92 million, reflecting benefits from the acquisition of Texas Instruments Inc's printer business.</p>
<p>In last year's fourth quarter, GENICOM reported earnings of $0.13 a share on sales of $75.6 million.  </p>
<p>GENICOM said its results for the quarter are expected to be released on or about February 4, 1997.</p>
<p>GENICOM purchased Texas Instruments's printer business for $27 million.</p>
